  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 200 PM MDT FRI SEP 25 2026\nTuesday looks breezy, dry, and slightly cooler as the next broad\nupper trough from the north Pacific comes inland and puts our \narea under strong zonal flow. Models continue in wide disagreement\nafter that with GFS steadily deepening the trough for continued\ncooling while ECM weakens the trough for gradual warming. Our \nforecast, based on NBM, favors the warmer ECM through Thursday, \nthen the cooler GFS Friday. The deeper and colder GFS will \nallow a slight chance of rain showers and even snow showers in \nthe central Idaho mountains on Friday.",
